shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.1=Use the set command to manage all Baritone settings. Nearly all behavior is controlled by these settings.
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.usage=Usage:
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.default=> set - Equivalent to 'set list'
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.list=> set list [page] - List all settings
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.modified=> set modified [page] - List modified settings
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.view=> set <setting> - View a setting's current value
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.set=> set <setting> <value> - Change a setting's value
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.reset_all=> set reset all - Reset all settings to their defaults
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.reset_one=> set reset <setting> - Reset a setting to its default
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.toggle=> set toggle <setting> - Toggle a boolean setting
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.save=> set save - Save all settings (usually saved automatically)
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.load=> set load - Load settings from setting.json
shadowbaritone.command.set.long_desc.example.load_file=> set load [filename] - Load another settings file from the shadowbaritone folder in the current configuration directory
